  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_029 (scvi_n200 + vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) at 0.7250 acc / 0.6847 F1. Across all 6 completed experiments, scvi_n200 >> scgpt, vit_l > resnet50, transformer > avgpool, and weighted ≥ concat. However, all experiments have been multiprofile; the singleprofile setting is completely unexplored. Question: Does removing the multiprofile aggregation step (singleprofile) with the best-known encoders (scvi_n200 + vit_l) and weighted fusion yield comparable or better accuracy at lower cost? This is the highest-value unexplored axis because it tests whether the aggregation overhead is actually contributing or whether a simpler single-profile pipeline with the same strong encoders can match or exceed 0.7250. If it matches, it is a cheaper solution; if it exceeds, it is a new best. It is the best use of experiment 7 because it reduces the largest remaining uncertainty (profile setting) while leveraging the strongest evidence for each component, and its expected cost is low (~2–3 GPU hours, no aggregation step), well below the multiprofile transformer configs, preserving budget for the remaining 3 experiments."
}

